{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Decision recorded: approach A + B APPROVED (operator authorization, 2026-09-01)\n\nThe operator approved BOTH parts of the durable fix as the direction. Implementation specifics (exact thresholds, code seams) proceed through the normal plan-review gate.\n\n**A — acute-pressure emergency reclaim tier.** Keep the 5 GB warm build-cache at normal disk levels, but above a hard threshold (~90% used, above the existing 80% soft `DISK_PRESSURE_PCT`) escalate `prune_docker_caches()` to `docker builder prune -f` with keep→0, and record bytes actually freed (not invocation count). Completes the documented intent of 28f9-535c (pressure-triggered prune), e2c5-f09b (5 GB cap), and applies 9bc0-1200's lesson (\"measure effect, not calls\"). OSS precedent: kubelet soft-vs-hard eviction thresholds; BuildKit GC keepBytes normally / aggressive prune under pressure.\n\n**B — near-full admission control in the review clone path.** Before materializing a snapshot (`src/rebar/llm/gate_source.py` / `src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py`), if free disk is below a hard floor, DEFER the review via ADR 0069's existing retryable-coverage-gap-bounded-deferral path (vote-less, budgeted) instead of cloning into ENOSPC. This prevents a self-inflicted disk-full from being misclassified as a `coverage-gap (review-error)` and burning the retry budget to a spurious fail-closed −1 (exactly what happened to change 2481 in this incident). OSS precedent: Jenkins disk-space node monitor (marks agent offline below threshold), Kubernetes ephemeral-storage eviction, Zuul executor disk governor.\n\n**Both, not one:** A frees space but a burst refills; B holds the line but leaves the disk pinned; together they self-heal. **EBS growth explicitly rejected** as the fix (workload-bound growth + %-based trigger → only delays the identical wall); acceptable only as a throwaway unwedge lever.\n\nDispatching an implementation agent to plan-review → claim → implement (held-out TDD) → land through Gerrit (LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1) → close."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788308413931818007,"uuid":"eb63f5b8-94a2-426f-ba78-541cf73808df"}